    "discipline": "momentum",
    "thesis": "This card exists to attribute a difference, not to win. It is Strategy B's rules -- the same ema(20)/ema(50) cross inside a close>sma(200) regime, the same 12% stop, the same 180-day cap, the same 6 slots at 15% -- pointed at a universe chosen by a rule instead of by an analyst. B-momentum's twelve names are a hand-picked AI and cloud-infrastructure book; this card's twelve are simply the most heavily traded index constituents with history back to 2004, ranked by median dollar volume over the design year and frozen. The two books overlap on the semiconductor complex and diverge everywhere else -- this one carries UNH, LLY and MSTR, which no thematic AI screen would have produced. If the wider store is worth having, a mechanical draw from it should not be far behind a curated one; if the curation was the whole edge, this card should underperform B materially and that is the finding. Note what this does and does not isolate: a twelve-name universe cannot be 'widened', only swapped, so this changes the universe and the selection method together. It does not claim to isolate breadth alone.",
